{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":51.65999984741211,"text":"The White Tower stands at the end of the seafront, round and thick, 34 meters tall. It was built around the 15th century, on the corner where the city walls met the sea, and it was part of the defenses. Later it became a prison, and in those years it was called by other names, much darker ones. The story people in Thessaloniki tell is that in the late 19th century, a prisoner offered to whitewash the whole thing in exchange for his freedom. Whether or not it happened that way, the tower was whitewashed, the name changed, and white it stayed even after the lime wore off. Today it holds nobody. Inside you climb a spiral ramp through six floors with the city museum around you, and come out on top to see the Thermaeic Gulf and, on clear days, Mount Olympus across the water.","words":[{"word":"The","start":0,"end":0.5400000214576721},{"word":"White","start":0.5400000214576721,"end":0.8600000143051147},{"word":"Tower","start":0.8600000143051147,"end":1.2000000476837158},{"word":"stands","start":1.2000000476837158,"end":1.659999966621399},{"word":"at","start":1.659999966621399,"end":1.8799999952316284},{"word":"the","start":1.8799999952316284,"end":2.200000047683716},{"word":"end","start":2.200000047683716,"end":2.240000009536743},{"word":"of","start":2.240000009536743,"end":2.440000057220459},{"word":"the","start":2.440000057220459,"end":2.559999942779541},{"word":"seafront","start":2.559999942779541,"end":2.9000000953674316},{"word":"round","start":3.880000114440918,"end":3.9000000953674316},{"word":"and","start":3.9000000953674316,"end":4.539999961853027},{"word":"thick","start":4.539999961853027,"end":4.539999961853027},{"word":"34","start":4.980000019073486,"end":5.420000076293945},{"word":"meters","start":5.420000076293945,"end":5.760000228881836},{"word":"tall","start":5.760000228881836,"end":6.159999847412109},{"word":"It","start":6.840000152587891,"end":6.940000057220459},{"word":"was",